--
-- The daily rite, from Sampradaya Vratha Pooja Vidhi (Giri), pp.27-51.
--
-- It is shaped differently from the other two poojas. Ganesha and Varalakshmi
-- are one deity with one sequence; this is FIVE deities in a fixed spatial
-- arrangement -- Shiva centre, Vishnu north-east, Surya south-east, Vinayaka
-- south-west, Devi north-west -- each invoked with its own VEDIC verse rather
-- than a puranic dhyana shloka, and each given its own archana with its own
-- flower. So there are five avahanams and five archanas, and deity_id names
-- the centre rather than the whole.
--
-- The purvangam is COPIED from the Ganesha pooja rather than re-derived. The
-- book does the same thing: page 29 lists the shared opening steps as page
-- references into the Purvanga section instead of reprinting them. A second
-- derivation would be a second copy that could drift from the first.
-- =============================================================================

